## Advanced Usage

### Custom Build Options

Run with custom image tag (preferred):

```bash
docker run --rm  \
-v "$(pwd):/data" \
--entrypoint=/bin/sh \
"registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:${VERSION}" \
-c "/data/buildPDF"
```

### Using Different Templates

Specify a different template:

```bash
--template=custom-template.tex
```

### Adding Filters

Add custom Pandoc filters in your defaults file:

```yaml
filters:
  - pandoc-plantuml
  - pandoc-mermaid-filter
```

## Docker Commands

### Pull the Image

Use a specific tag by exporting `VERSION` before running the commands below.

```bash
docker pull registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:${VERSION}
```

### Run Manually

```bash
docker run --rm  \
-v "$(pwd):/data" \
--entrypoint=/bin/sh \
"registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:${VERSION}" \
-c "/data/buildPDF"
```

## Troubleshooting

### Docker Issues

- Ensure Docker is running: `docker ps`
- Check image exists: `docker images | grep pandoc`

### Build Errors

- Check file permissions: `ls -la {{DOCS_DIR}}/`
- Verify markdown syntax in your files
- Check logs in terminal output

### Font Issues

- List available fonts: `fc-list`
- Modify font settings in metadata.yaml

